nCandidate B: very conscientious, handles stress very well, good at assessing weather, excellent computer skills. Concerns: relatively weak memory for numbers, makes nasty remarks about colleagues. Strengths: reliability (conscientious), stress resilience, technical (weather, computer). Concerns: crew cooperation (nasty remarks), attention (weak memory for numbers). So issues.\n\nCandidate C: can make correct decisions quickly, keeps calm in crisis, understands complicated technology. Concerns: difficulty communicating ideas, regarded as egocentric, not willing to further education. Strengths: decision quality, stress resilience, technical competence. Concerns: crew cooperation, adaptability/feedback orientation.\n\nCandidate D: responds to unexpected events adequately, can concentrate very well, solves problems extremely well, takes responsibility seriously. Concerns: regarded as know-it-all, hot temper. Strengths: reliability, attention, problem solving, responsibility. Concerns: crew cooperation (know-it-all, hot temper). No explicit stress resilience but responds to unexpected events adequately.\n\nWe need to pick best overall fit. All have some concerns. Which candidate has strongest overall? Let's weigh.\n\nCandidate C has strong decision making, calm under crisis, technical, but communication issues and egocentric, not willing to further education. That is serious for crew cooperation and adaptability.\n\nCandidate D has strong problem solving, concentration, responsibility, but hot temper and know-it-all may affect crew cooperation. No explicit stress resilience but can respond to unexpected events adequately (maybe okay). No mention of technical competence beyond problem solving; but solves problems extremely well suggests technical.\n\nCandidate B has stress handling, conscientiousness, weather assessment, computer skills, but nasty remarks and weak memory for numbers. Memory for numbers important for flight data. Nasty remarks affect crew cooperation.\n\nCandidate A has anticipation, complex connections, spatial vision, leadership, but show-off and not open to new ideas. Leadership good, but show-off may affect crew.\n\nWhich is best? Possibly Candidate D because responsibility, concentration, problem solving, and ability to respond to unexpected events are crucial. The hot temper and know-it-all are concerns but maybe manageable. Candidate B's nasty remarks are severe for crew cooperation. Candidate C's egocentric and communication issues also severe. Candidate A's show-off may be less severe than hot temper? Hard.\n\nI think D is strongest overall: high reliability, attention, problem solving, responsibility, and adequate stress response. So I will recommend Candidate D.\n\nNow need to reference existing discussion: none, but can say \"Given we have not yet discussed candidates, I propose we start with Candidate D as leading.\" Provide evidence.\n\nPublic message: state recommendation, give evidence, explain why D stands out compared to others.\n\nMetadata vote: Candidate D.\n\nProceed."}
